# Isolated controls: pre-audit admission tests must assert durable state, not wording
#
# Requirement under test (verification contract): "above-target eligible
# pre-audit/dispatch boundaries invoke safe compaction or retain durable
# recovery when unavailable/failed; in-flight audits are not disrupted, and
# completion/recovery reaches the next safe compaction boundary without lost or
# duplicate work" — demonstrated by isolated controls that "do not rely on
# incidental object identity, wording or test totals".
#
# The previous tests asserted two human-facing strings:
#   assert.match(result.content[0]!.text, /AUDIT PENDING/);
#   assert.match(buildWidgetLines(...), /waiting for safe compaction boundary/);
# These pin diagnostic English and widget copy, so a harmless rewording failed
# the suite while the protected behavior was intact.
#
# Control surface: disposable copy /tmp/glla-p1 (since removed), carrying
# extensions/, scripts/, tests/, package.json, tsconfig.json, bunfig.toml and a
# symlinked node_modules. bunfig.toml is required: its [test] preload
# (./tests/harness/setup.ts) provides the hermetic global-settings redirect,
# and without it even an unmodified copy fails on ctx.modelRegistry.find.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BASELINE (unmodified copy):
#    11 pass
#     0 fail
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONTROL A — harmless rewording must PASS (behavior untouched).
# Reworded the pre-audit response text in extensions/loops/goal-tools.ts and
# BOTH widget phase labels in extensions/goal-loop-display.ts
# ("waiting for safe compaction boundary" -> "holding for a safe compaction
# boundary"):
#   "AUDIT PENDING — nonterminal. ..."
#     -> "Detached audit queued — not yet terminal. Claim persisted; a
#         preventive compaction check runs at the next owned idle boundary.
#         Stop here."
#
#    11 pass
#     0 fail
#   control-A-exit=0
#
# RESULT: correctly PASSES. Neither response copy nor widget copy is a load-
# bearing requirement; the suite now asserts behavior instead of prose. Under
# the previous assertions this exact edit failed 3 tests (the auditor reported
# `/AUDIT PENDING/` and `/waiting for safe compaction boundary/` mismatches).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONTROL B — removing the admission guard must FAIL on DURABLE state.
# Deleted the `if (preventiveCompactionDue(ctx)) { ... return staged }` block so
# completion dispatches immediately inside the still-busy tool callback instead
# of staging revision-bound admission debt for an owned idle boundary. This is
# the actual regression the objective repairs.
#
#   71 |  assert.equal(staged.pendingCompletion?.preAuditCompaction, true);
#       |         ^ AssertionError: Expected values to be strictly equal:
#   (fail) busy complete_goal stages admission, then success launches exactly one stored audit
#   (fail) busy complete_goal stages admission, then failure launches exactly one stored audit
#   (fail) busy complete_goal stages admission, then unavailable launches exactly one stored audit
#   (fail) late compaction callbacks cannot dispatch across revision change
#   (fail) late compaction callbacks cannot dispatch across cancel change
#   control-B-exit=1
#
# RESULT: correctly FAILS, and it fails on the DURABLE admission assertion
# (pendingCompletion.preAuditCompaction), not on any message text — proving the
# replacement assertions still detect the meaningful regression.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Live repository source (unmodified): tests/pre-audit-compaction.test.ts runs
# 11 passed / 0 failed. Retained coverage: durable staged admission
# (preAuditCompaction + stored attemptId), no worker before owned idle
# admission, a falsely settled busy host stays held, exactly-once compaction
# and exactly-once audit dispatch across success/failure/unavailable, no audit
# overlapping compaction, preserved claim summary/objective/contract after
# admission, no extra main-agent turn, and decision/cold-load/cancel/revision/
# session/owner gating. A grep of both amended test files for the former
# wording patterns returns no matches.
